From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:30:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 187/207] dsv41: project abstain anchors into the reply's final
 fields

The runner records abstain anchors in its raw field bytes. The HTTP reply trims the newlines after the think close
and pyStrips whole-reply reasoning, so the anchors pointed past the final text. T5's case is raw content byte 12
against final byte 10.

With abstain records on, generation.finish now writes runner.field_projection per field (raw_bytes, dropped_lead,
final_bytes), each cell's final_at, and abstain source/close/resume anchors in final bytes. The raw values are kept
as raw_*. Streamed replies are mapped against the fields their deltas sent. An anchor in a dropped head or tail is
null. Receipts without abstain records are unchanged.

test-runner-projection-host: T5's counterexample through openai.run, whole and streamed; the reasoning strip; the
off identity.

(cherry picked from commit 7f32fcd286fa6160fec15ff1624686f409835323)
